menu "Status LED Configuration"

    config STATUS_LED_WS2812
        bool "Use a WS2812 (NeoPixel) RGB LED for status"
        default n
        help
            Drive a single addressable WS2812 RGB LED as the status indicator
            instead of the three discrete GPIO activity LEDs. The color encodes
            the bridge mode: solid green = idle (no host), breathing green =
            ready, blue = flashing, purple = JTAG/SWD debug, fast red blink =
            fatal error; brief blue/cyan blips show bridge<->target traffic.

    config STATUS_LED_GPIO
        int "WS2812 data GPIO"
        depends on STATUS_LED_WS2812
        default 21
        help
            GPIO connected to the WS2812 data-in. On the Waveshare ESP32-S3-Zero
            the onboard RGB LED is on GPIO21.

    config STATUS_LED_BRIGHTNESS
        int "WS2812 brightness percent (1-100)"
        depends on STATUS_LED_WS2812
        range 1 100
        default 20
        help
            Global brightness scaling applied to every color. WS2812s are very
            bright; 20% is usually plenty for an indicator.

endmenu
